###1) Completing the square

The number that will help us complete the square is $\left(\dfrac{\blueD{16}}{2}\right)^2=\goldD{64}$:

$\begin{align}
x^2+\blueD{16}x&=13
\\\\
x^2+\blueD{16}x+\goldD{64}&=77&&\text{Add 64.}
\\\\
(x+8)^2&=77&&\text{Factor.}
\end{align}$

[[☃ explanation 1]]

###2) Solving the equation

$\begin{align}
(x+8)^2&=77
\\\\
\sqrt{(x+8)^2}&=\pm\sqrt{77}&&\text{Take the square root.}
\\\\
x+8&= \pm \sqrt{77}
\\\\
x&= -8 \pm \sqrt{77}&&\text{Subtract }8.
\end{align}$
